			"notes": "Adds separate uploads for activity-specific resource packs while preserving the existing Polymer main-pack URL.\n\n### Added\n- Named resource packs with independent, content-addressed R2 object keys, e.g. `destiny/exodus_crash+<sha1>.zip`.\n- Optional `additionalPacks` configuration, uploaded after successful main-pack generation/upload.\n- `uploadR2ResourcePacks` task for uploading the main pack and configured activity packs together.\n- `-PpackId=...` for uploading a single named pack.\n- Public `R2ResourcePackUpload.uploadPack(packId, path)` API returning the published URL, SHA-1 and size only after a successful upload.\n- Validation for duplicate/reserved IDs and invalid path segments.\n\n### Compatibility\n- Minecraft 26.3, Java 25 and Fabric.\n- Existing credential configuration and main-pack path remain supported; `additionalPacks` defaults to an empty list.\n- Activity ZIP generation/splitting and player entry/exit pack switching are handled by the consuming game mod, not this uploader.\n\n### Validation\n- Gradle `build` passed, including `verifyR2Uploader`.\n- Local HTTP checks cover signed main/activity-pack paths, uploaded bytes, DNS failover, HTTP failures and redirect rejection.\n- Manual task checks confirm missing activity files and invalid pack IDs fail before upload.\n- Actual Cloudflare R2 uploads and in-game activity switching were not exercised for this release."
		},
